
==================== RUNNING trial-081 (esm2_t33_650M_aspect_prediction: same full budget as trial-080, plus --mask-sparse-negatives-max-total-terms 2 (Open World Assumption mitigation)) ====================

note: Identical to trial-080 in every hyperparameter, with one addition: --mask-sparse-negatives-max-total-terms 2. trial-080 (full 6000-train/1000-val/8-epoch budget, no masking) confirmed real learning (AUROC up 12-21% relative over trial-079's health check) but hit a much lower ceiling than every other task in this sweep (pooled AUROC 0.6844 vs ~0.94-0.96 elsewhere) and showed clean, textbook OVERFITTING past epoch 4. Investigation (see experiments/sweep_log.md) confirmed why: proteins missing a given aspect are systematically under-annotated everywhere (63-75% have <=2 total GO terms across their entire record, vs a full-dataset median of 4) - matching GO's own documented 'Open World Assumption'. This trial tests the agreed mitigation: exclude 'negative' aspect labels from the loss (both training and validation-for-best-checkpoint-selection) when the protein's total_terms is <=2. Positive labels are always trusted regardless of total_terms. --run-diagnostic stays deliberately UNMASKED so the two trials' AUROC numbers remain directly comparable. --push-to-hub NOT set. Fresh start from facebook/esm2_t33_650M_UR50D.
